docs(framework): close Baton Track A item A4 in CLI reference; bump fw 4.38.1 -> 4.39.0

The 4.38.0 graduation shipped the work_verb/design_provenance fields into
the templates, the charter schema, and straymark validate — but Track A
item A4 ("Update docs/adopters/CLI-REFERENCE.md with the new fields")
never landed. The reference adopters consult for the fields their
templates now carry said nothing about them. This commit closes that gap
and bumps the Framework to 4.39.0, packaging the Track C adopter kit in
the same release note.

== CLI-REFERENCE.md x3 locales (EN/es/zh-CN) ==

Two insertions per locale:

straymark validate — the advisory work-classification vocabulary check:
charter frontmatter and follow-up backlog entries are checked against the
controlled vocabulary (design/implement/audit/operate; new/upstream).
Absent fields emit nothing — undeclared is an honest state, never an
error; out-of-vocabulary values emit a warning that never blocks.

straymark charter new — the two optional declared work-classification
frontmatter fields, with the load-bearing determination rules: defining a
bounded foundational contract is implement, NOT design; and implement +
design_provenance: upstream (only instruments prior design) degrades to
mechanical work. Undeclared Charters route conservatively to frontier.

